  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 1255 AM CDT Mon Aug 10 2026\n\nAs the upper ridge continues slowly drifting towards the southeast, \ntemperatures will continue to increase a little more each day into \nnext week before peaking by late week. Air temperatures during this \nstretch are forecast to reach the 100-102 degree range for many \nareas every day. These higher temperatures combined with the \nhumidity may produce Heat Advisory criteria (108 degrees or higher) \nfor areas mainly east of I-37/I-35. The hot and mainly dry weather \nlooks to stick around heading into next weekend. Humidity values \nshould be a touch lower along with high temps mainly in the upper \n90s so we should stay just shy of heat advisory criteria during this \nstretch however it will still continue to be quite hot across the \narea. Continue to check back for updates and remember to practice \nsafe heat safety.",
